    { "key": "rite.title", "section": "The Rite", "what": "Salt bowl heading", "copy": "An offering, an inheritance" },
    { "key": "rite.body", "section": "The Rite", "what": "Salt bowl explanation", "copy": "Salt preserves. For as long as people have made promises, it has sealed them. At the reception, a bowl will be waiting. Add a pinch of salt ⟨provided, or bring your own?⟩, and with it a piece of wisdom for the marriage: a line, a warning, a recipe, a blessing. The bowl goes home with them and keeps." },

